---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/ui/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const lastUpdated = '2026-10-14';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: "Chere' support", path: '/chere/support' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Chere' Support · Winters Code"
  description="Help with the Chere' app: joining the beta, connecting your phone to your business, a lost phone, and how to reach the person who builds it."
  canonicalPath="/chere/support"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema(crumbs))} />
  </Fragment>

  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />

  <article class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-eyebrow mono">CHERE' · SUPPORT</div>
    <h1 class="h1 legal-h1">Help is just a text away.</h1>
    <p class="legal-tagline">
      Chere' is built and kept running by one person in Bandon. When something's off, you
      reach me, not a ticket queue.
    </p>
    <p class="small legal-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <p class="legal-lead">
        Text <a href="sms:5415510731">541-551-0731</a> or email
        <a href="mailto:preston@winterscode.com">preston@winterscode.com</a>. Tell me what you
        were doing and what you saw. A screenshot helps.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Joining the beta on iPhone</h2>
      <ol class="support-steps">
        <li>Install Apple's free TestFlight app from the App Store.</li>
        <li>Open the invite I send you, then tap Accept and Install.</li>
        <li>Open Chere' and connect your phone, below.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>On Android, text me and I'll get Chere' onto your phone.</p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Connecting your phone to your business</h2>
      <ol class="support-steps">
        <li>Open Chere'. It shows a short key for this phone.</li>
        <li>Text me that key. It is not a password, so texting it is fine.</li>
        <li>
          I text back a one-time setup code. It works once, for that phone only, and it
          doesn't last long, so type it in when it arrives.
        </li>
        <li>Type the code into Chere', and your phone is connected to your business.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">A lost or replaced phone</h2>
      <p>
        Text me. I cut the old phone off from your business's server, so it can't sign in to
        your records again. What it had saved for working offline stays behind the app's own
        lock. Then connect the new phone the same way as above.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Sending feedback during the beta</h2>
      <p>
        Take a screenshot while you're in Chere' and TestFlight offers to send it to me with a
        note. You can also open TestFlight and tap Send Beta Feedback. Or just text me.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Working without signal</h2>
      <p>
        Your recent records are kept on the phone, so you can look things up on a job site
        with no bars. Changes you make wait on the phone and go to your business's server once
        you're back online.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2 legal-h2">Your data</h2>
      <p>
        What Chere' keeps, where it goes and how to have it deleted is all in the
        <a href="/chere/privacy">Chere' privacy policy</a>. To get a copy of your records or
        have them deleted, text or email me.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 4px 64px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) {
    .legal-page {
      padding: 64px 4px 80px;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-page {
      padding: 80px 0 96px;
    }
  }

  .legal-eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-copper);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) {
    .legal-eyebrow { font-size: 12px; }
  }

  .legal-h1 {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  .legal-tagline {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--color-ash-300);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    max-width: 600px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-tagline { font-size: 19px; }
  }

  .legal-updated {
    margin-top: 8px;
    color: var(--color-ash-500);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .legal-body {
    margin-top: 36px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
    color: var(--color-ash-300);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-body { font-size: 16px; }
  }
  .legal-body p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal-lead {
    padding: 16px 18px;
    background: rgba(77, 216, 168, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid rgba(77, 216, 168, 0.25);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    color: var(--color-ash-100);
    font-style: italic;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 16px !important;
    line-height: 1.6 !important;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .legal-lead {
      font-size: 18px !important;
      padding: 20px 24px;
    }
  }

  .legal-h2 {
    margin-top: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) {
    .legal-h2 { margin-top: 28px; }
  }

  .legal-body a {
    color: var(--color-copper-bright);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--copper-hairline);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  @media (hover: hover) {

    .legal-body a:hover {
    color: var(--color-wc-green);
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-wc-green-dim);
  }}

  .support-steps {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .support-steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
    padding-left: 26px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .support-steps li::before {
    content: counter(step) '.';
    position: absolute;
    left: 2px;
    top: 0;
    color: var(--color-copper);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
